                <pb facs="0333" n="249" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg249"/>

                <head>No. 102.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Reinberg to Mr. Porter.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Guayaquil, Ecuador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-04-30"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 30, 1885</date>.
                        (Received May 18.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 120.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose yon herewith
                    five declarations relative to the case of Julio Romano Santos. Of these
                    affidavits two were forwarded by Consular Agent Goddard, and the three others
                    were duly declared before me in this consular office.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>MARTIN REINBERG.</signed></closer>







